            {
                "box": {
                    "bgcolor": [ 0.25098039215686274, 0.3215686274509804, 0.4196078431372549, 1.0 ],
                    "color": [ 0.34509803921568627, 0.42745098039215684, 0.5333333333333333, 1.0 ],
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "notes",
                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                    "numinlets": 0,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patcher": {
                        "fileversion": 1,
                        "appversion": {
                            "major": 9,
                            "minor": 2,
                            "revision": 1,
                            "architecture": "x64",
                            "modernui": 1
                        },
                        "classnamespace": "box",
                        "rect": [ 80.0, 100.0, 1020.0, 820.0 ],
                        "boxes": [
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "fontsize": 13.0,
                                    "id": "notes",
                                    "linecount": 31,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 20.0, 20.0, 978.0, 750.0 ],
                                    "text": "NUMBERED PRESETS\nChoose PRESET # (1–128), then STORE to capture or RECALL to load. Changing the number alone does nothing to the sound.\nSTORE replaces only the selected slot. Wait for “Stored preset N,” then Cmd+S to keep the entire bank in this patch. An incomplete capture does not overwrite a slot.\nPreset 1 starts with the supplied sound; slots 2–128 are empty. The displayed last-stored and last-recalled numbers identify each action.\nSaved: SPAT oper scene, renderer state and binaural HRTF/ITD/listener/rendering state. The 8-channel mix and stereo headphone live.gain~ faders are exclusively user controls; STORE, RECALL and startup preset recall do not query or change them. The capture inputs filter /dsp/latency and convert other Max OSC messages into FullPacket before o.dict.\nMONITOR remains independent and opens in Room (2). DSP, recording and sample playback are independent.\nThe last stored or recalled preset is restored on reopening. Code and all occupied slots are embedded in Preset_STORAGE.\n\nMULTICHANNEL / HEADPHONE REFERENCE\nThe common eight-channel signal after COMMON MIX GAIN feeds room monitoring, the eight-channel recorder and the binaural renderer. Binaural source n is virtual loudspeaker n. No second reverb is added.\nRecall restores renderer and binaural settings first, then the oper scene and an oper bang. The speaker adapter regenerates headphone-source positions from the recalled speaker layout. Eight sources, eight speakers and one room are fixed by this patch.\nThe supplied layout is a 1 m horizontal ring at -45, 0, 45, 90, 135, 180, -135 and -90 degrees; the factory HRTF is KEMAR. Custom HRTF files must remain available on disk.\n\nNAMED AUDIO BUSES / COPYING\nEach mono playlist feeds one s~ Spat5_1 through s~ Spat5_8. The corresponding r~ objects directly above spat5.spat~ feed inputs 1 through 8 in the same order. The trajectory generator and its controls have been removed.\nCopy the framed core to carry the receivers, preset bank, speaker adapter, monitor router, initialization and recording. Feed the matching send names from any source patch. All supporting patchers and bank code are embedded. No presentation mode is used.\n\nCHECK IN MAX\nOpen with Max 9, SPAT5 and CNMAT odot installed. Store two different source positions / room settings into different numbers. Set the two live.gain~ faders by hand, recall each preset and verify the SPAT state changes while both faders remain at the levels you chose. Cmd+S, close and reopen to check bank persistence.\nHeadphones routes only to outputs 1–2; Room routes all eight common feeds. Check speaker channel order and levels in the actual room. Generic HRTFs are a speaker-feed preview, not a measured reproduction of that room.\nOffline validation covers wiring and bank behavior. Live SPAT acceptance, sound and headphone-to-room matching still need checking in Max. The eight players now reference the supplied audio files beside this patch. Keep the extracted folder together."
                                }
                            }
                        ],
                        "lines": [],
